Check what you have before cooking, crafting, or selling, without searching every cabinet. Since game 1.1.19611 the game shows this count in the storage, shop, and trade windows; Item Totals shows it in every other window with item tooltips.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*]Shows the game's own line [font=Courier New]Usable at home: N[/font], in its green, in the item tooltips of the cooking window, the workbench, the material rack, the brewing, dye, and Rat Cage windows, the other station windows, and the item detail popup.[/*]
[*]Adds nothing where the game already shows its line, so you never see two numbers.[/*]
[*]Counts what the game counts: your backpack and the home storage you can access. A Brewing Barrel, a locked bag, a shredder hopper, a compressor bin, and a dye vat are left out, as in the game.[/*]
[*]Uses the game's own text, so it follows the game's language, also a community language pack.[/*]
[*]Adds nothing to your save; safe to remove at any time.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*]Survival Log 1.1.19611 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Install it first.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\ItemTotals.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]ItemTotals.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

